<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 220)</h2>
<p><b>Many voices, one document.</b> Built for the agency-review call: five people, five places, one transcript.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Notes sync the moment they're made</b> — typed notes instantly, voice notes as soon as their transcript lands. Every note carries its author, frame and timecode, and the host's single <b>Export Note Report</b> holds everyone's.</li>
<li><b>Simultaneous markup is safe.</b> Two people finishing strokes on the same frame at the same moment now both keep both marks — previously the two lists swapped and each person lost their own stroke.</li>
<li>Each reviewer runs their own Asobi with their own mic, so every voice transcribes cleanly under its own name — no untangling a shared recording.</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Everyone updates together:</b> this build speaks sync protocol 3. Older copies in a shared review are told to update rather than silently drifting.</p>
]]></description>
