<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 218)</h2>
<p><b>Publish back to Kitsu, and the G filmstrip.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>File ▸ Publish Review to Kitsu…</b> — the clip's notes become a comment on its task, with your name, frames and timecode. Flip the status in your studio's own vocabulary, attach the <b>marked-up frames</b> (on by default) and optionally the burned-in movie. The Publish button names the project it writes to.</li>
<li>Asobi ignores its own published attachments when pulling, so a review movie never comes back pretending to be a new artist version.</li>
<li><b>Press G</b> — the playlist as thumbnails over the viewport. Any playlist, any source. Mid-shot posters, click to jump, current clip ringed, S/M/L sizes where <b>large is a grid</b>.</li>
<li>The playlist panel can show the same thumbnails — the photo button in its header.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
