<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 215)</h2>
<p><b>Flip to source.</b> Check the QuickTimes for pace; judge the pixels on the real thing.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>⌥⌘F</b> swaps a clip pulled from Kitsu for the original render named in its upload comment — and back. Notes, grades and annotations follow the clip across the flip.</li>
<li>Colour follows the media: the preview plays Rec.709, the EXR plates it came from play ACEScg.</li>
<li>Comments that record project-relative paths need the <b>source root</b> set once in the Kitsu panel (your pipeline's <code>proj</code> folder).</li>
<li>If the comment names no source, or the path isn't reachable from this Mac, Asobi <b>says so plainly</b> — it never guesses at media.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
